ue,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Neptune Insurance Holdings Inc., through its subsidiary, Neptune Flood Incorporated, operates as an insurance agency that engages in selling residential and commercial flood insurance policies on behalf of insurance carrier partners in the United States. The company offers primary and excess flood, parametric earthquake, and indemnity earthquake insurance through a network of agencies. Neptune Insurance Holdings Inc. was founded in 2016 and is based in Saint Petersburg, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Trevor R. Burgess | CEO & Chairman | Age 52 | Compensation: $414,300 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 62 people. Revenue per employee of $2.6M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $770K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $184K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Neptune Insurance Holdings Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.8B market cap on $160M of annual revenue.","The business throws off $48M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.38\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 3.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 22% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 355% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.5528763547459064},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $28.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 15% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Is Neptune Insurance Holdings Inc. (NP) Up 2.2% Since Last Earnings Report?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3032641/why-is-neptune-insurance-holdings-inc-np-up-2-2-since-last-earnings-report?cid=CS-ZC-FT-realtime_blog-3032641","date":"20